rivoli is an independent implementation written from scratch in Rust. It
is not a fork or a derivative distribution of colibri, and contains no
copied colibri source. colibri's `glm.c` was consulted as a reference
oracle to validate numerical parity (int4 snapshot layout, MoE gating,
and attention row projection), and rivoli reads colibri's on-disk int4
snapshot and usage-ranking file formats so that artifacts transfer
between the two engines.

Credit to the colibri authors for demonstrating that a 744B
mixture-of-experts model can be decoded on consumer hardware, and for
publishing the work openly.
